   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 511 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law relating\nto the imposition of an occupancy tax on the village of Mount Kisco, in\nrelation to extending the provisions of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S8865",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8865-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 511 of 2016",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8865\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 511 of the laws of 2016, amending the tax law\nrelating to the imposition of an occupancy tax on the village of Mount\nKisco, in relation to extending the provisions of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nExtends provisions relating to the imposition of an occupancy tax on the\nvillage of Mount Kisco until September 1, 2025\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 extends the expiration date of chapter 511 of the laws of 2018\nfrom September 1, 2022, to September 1, 2025.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Village of Mount Kisco has requested the introduction of this legis-\nlation to extend the authorization for the village to extend its 3%\ndaily room tax on any room in a hotel, motel, or similar place.  This\ntax has been used to raise revenues to support municipal expenses and\nwill continue as such.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
